Negative control for the reshaped `createTraceabilityCheck` (the PARTIAL verdict).

Withdraws the partial verdict by widening the not-yet arm from "none of the
scenario's own steps matched" to "not all of them matched". A scenario matched
only in PART — the dangerous case, because it reads as driveable and silently is
not — is then graded `notYet` instead of `partial`, so `partial` is empty for
every input and the assertion that guards it can never fail.

The assertion that must go RED: the one asserting `partial` is empty over a
feature holding a half-matched scenario.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Proven RED 2026-08-12, blind
(`pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/scenario-harness exec vitest run src/steps/__tests__/traceability.test.ts`):
  x FAILS a scenario matched only in part — the case that reads driveable and silently is not
      -> expected [] to strictly equal [ 'half driveable' ]
  x PASSES a scenario no step matches at all — a capability written down and not yet driven
      -> expected [ 'half driveable', 'not driveable at all' ] to strictly equal [ 'not driveable at all' ]
  2 failed | 11 passed. Reverted with `git apply -R`; suite back to 13 passed.

Behaviour shift measured by the author (NOT the red proof) — over a feature with
one half-matched and one unmatched scenario:
  before: partial = ["half driveable"], notYet = ["not driveable at all"]
  after:  partial = [],                 notYet = ["half driveable", "not driveable at all"]

diff --git a/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts b/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts
--- a/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts
+++ b/packages/scenario-harness/src/steps/traceability.ts
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@ export function createTraceabilityCheck(
     const matched = map(scenario.steps, isMatched);
     const ownMatched = drop(matched, scenario.backgroundStepCount);
 
-    const verdict: Verdict = !some(ownMatched)
+    const verdict: Verdict = !every(ownMatched)
       ? VERDICT.NOT_YET
       : every(matched)
         ? VERDICT.DRIVEABLE
